---
import Section from "#/components/ui/Section.astro";
import Heading from "#/components/ui/Heading.astro";
import Paragraph from "#/components/ui/Paragraph.astro";
import Content from "#/components/ui/Content.astro";
import Highlight from "#/components/ui/Highlight.astro";
import FaqItem from "#/components/ui/FaqItem.astro";
---

<Section variant="light" headingId="faqHeading" descriptionId="faqDescription">
    <Content slot="text">
        <Heading id="faqHeading"> Frequently asked questions </Heading>
        <Paragraph id="faqDescription"
            >Can't find your answer? We can help you in the <a
                href="https://discord.gg/THRnn8fhkZ"
                target="_blank"
                class="text-bubblegum-pink"
                rel="noopener noreferrer">Support server</a
            >
        </Paragraph>
        <ul class="mt-3 grid grid-cols-1 gap-5 gap-x-7 lg:grid-cols-2">
            <FaqItem headingId="iAddedTheBotWhatNowHeading" descriptionId="iAddedTheBotWhatNowDescription">
                <Heading variant="h3" id="iAddedTheBotWhatNowHeading">I added the bot, what now?</Heading>
                <Paragraph classes="text-base font-medium" id="iAddedTheBotWhatNowDescription">
                    <Highlight color="text-bubblegum-pink font-bold">Run /enable in a channel.</Highlight> The bot will start
                    learning from new messages there. After chatting for a bit run /meme to generate a meme. Memes will also
                    come automatically when the channel is active and there is a conversation ongoing. You can change frequency
                    for those in /settings.
                </Paragraph>
            </FaqItem>
            <FaqItem headingId="canIHaveDifferentSettingsHeading" descriptionId="canIHaveDifferentSettingsDescription">
                <Heading variant="h3" id="canIHaveDifferentSettingsHeading"
                    >Can I have different settings for every channel?</Heading
                >
                <Paragraph classes="text-base font-medium" id="canIHaveDifferentSettingsDescription">
                    <Highlight color="text-bubblegum-pink font-bold">Yes!</Highlight> All channel information, such as data
                    for memes, frequency and other settings are stored separately for each channel. Nothing stops you from
                    having very low meme frequency in your main chat, but also set it to high in your flood channel.
                </Paragraph>
            </FaqItem>
            <FaqItem headingId="isThereALimitOnMemesHeading" descriptionId="isThereALimitOnMemesDescription">
                <Heading variant="h3" id="isThereALimitOnMemesHeading"
                    >Is there a limit on how many memes the bot can make daily?</Heading
                >
                <Paragraph classes="text-base font-medium" id="isThereALimitOnMemesDescription">
                    <Highlight color="text-bubblegum-pink font-bold">No, there are no limits.</Highlight> You can run /meme
                    as many times a day as you want. And it's free, because each generation only takes milliseconds to finish.
                </Paragraph>
            </FaqItem>
            <FaqItem headingId="canIDeleteStoredDataHeading" descriptionId="canIDeleteStoredDataDescription">
                <Heading variant="h3" id="canIDeleteStoredDataHeading"
                    >Can I delete stored meme generation data?</Heading
                >
                <Paragraph classes="text-base font-medium" id="canIDeleteStoredDataDescription">
                    <Highlight color="text-bubblegum-pink font-bold">Yes, at any time.</Highlight> Run /settings and then
                    press the "Delete all data" button to delete everything that the bot stored for the channel.
                </Paragraph>
            </FaqItem>
        </ul>
    </Content>
</Section>
